"answer": "Project Zenith is an AI-driven initiative focused on data analytics, predictive analytics in aerospace, and satellite communication systems. Key milestones include a kick-off on June 15th with a $500,000 phase one budget (later expanded to a $2M total budget approved by the executive board). Initial findings suggest a 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms. The project involves team expansions, including five new members in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, and a call for R&D ideas by July 20th. A prototype for secure file sharing was successfully tested ahead of schedule, leading to a celebration of the testing phase completion on October 10th. Future plans include user interface enhancements in October and updated security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January next year."
